# VO5C P4B15/R2 — illustrative OS privilege boundary (install manually after SRE review).
# Script guards alone do not stop unrestricted root.
#
# Goals:
# - Routine deploy role cannot invoke promotion scripts except pinned runner.
# - sudo preserves a sanitized environment (no caller-controlled SYNQDRIVE_* injection).
#
# 1) Deploy service account (example): synqdrive-deploy
# 2) Root-owned immutable pinned executor tree (chmod -R a-w, root:root)
# 3) Authority file /opt/synqdrive/shared/vo5c-production-deploy-authority.env root:root 0444
# 4) Wrapper script root:root 0755 that exports only fixed pins before exec:
#      /opt/synqdrive/shared/bin/vo5c-pinned-deploy-wrapper.sh
#
# Example sudoers fragment (validate with visudo):
#
# Defaults:synqdrive-deploy env_reset
# Defaults:synqdrive-deploy secure_path="/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin"
# Defaults:synqdrive-deploy !setenv
#
# synqdrive-deploy ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/synqdrive/shared/bin/vo5c-pinned-deploy-wrapper.sh
#
# Deny direct promotion entrypoints at the OS layer (chmod 0750 root:vo5c-breakglass or absent from PATH):
#   /opt/synqdrive/current/backend/scripts/ops/vps-deploy-release.sh
#   /opt/synqdrive/current/backend/scripts/ops/vps-deploy-connectivity-staging.sh
#   shallow-fetch cloud-agent deploy paths
#
# Emergency containment (class E) remains root-only / break-glass:
#   pm2 stop, di-v0-s4-gate6-open-rekill-production.sh, rfrf-production-rollback.sh
# RFRF safety rollback (class C) is NOT blocked by deploy enforcement.
